📘 Kubernetes + Istio + Knative Setup Guide
1️⃣ Prerequisites
Kubernetes cluster (v1.32.x)
1 master + 2 workers
Container runtime: containerd
CNI: Calico
2️⃣ Install Cert Manager
kubectl get pods -n cert-manager

✔ Ensure:

cert-manager
cert-manager-cainjector
cert-manager-webhook → Running
3️⃣ Install Istio
istioctl install --set profile=demo -y
⚠️ Fix Calico Issue

Edit Felix config:

kubectl edit felixconfiguration default

Set:

bpfConnectTimeLoadBalancing: Disabled

Restart calico:

kubectl delete pod -n calico-system -l k8s-app=calico-node
✅ Verify Istio
kubectl get pods -n istio-system

✔ Expect:

istiod
istio-ingressgateway
istio-egressgateway
4️⃣ Install Knative Serving
⚠️ Important Issue You Faced

Latest Knative requires:
👉 Kubernetes ≥ 1.33
But your cluster is:
👉 1.32

✅ Solution: Use compatible version
kubectl apply -f https://github.com/knative/serving/releases/download/knative-v1.14.0/serving-crds.yaml

kubectl apply -f https://github.com/knative/serving/releases/download/knative-v1.14.0/serving-core.yaml
5️⃣ Enable Istio Injection
kubectl label namespace knative-serving istio-injection=enabled --overwrite
6️⃣ Install Knative Istio Networking
kubectl apply -f https://github.com/knative/net-istio/releases/download/knative-v1.14.0/net-istio.yaml
✅ Verify Knative
kubectl get pods -n knative-serving

✔ All should be Running

7️⃣ Deploy Sample App
kubectl apply -f - <<EOF
apiVersion: serving.knative.dev/v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: hello
  namespace: default
spec:
  template:
    spec:
      containers:
        - image: gcr.io/knative-samples/helloworld-go
          env:
            - name: TARGET
              value: "Knative"
EOF
8️⃣ Get Service URL
kubectl get ksvc hello

Example:

http://hello.default.<EXTERNAL-IP>.nip.io
9️⃣ Access Application
curl http://hello.default.<EXTERNAL-IP>.nip.io

✔ Output:

Hello Knative!
🔟 Update Application (New Revision)
kubectl edit ksvc hello

Change:

value: "Knative v2!"
Verify revisions
kubectl get revisions
1️⃣1️⃣ Traffic Splitting

Edit service:

kubectl edit ksvc hello

Set:

traffic:
- revisionName: hello-00001
  percent: 50
- revisionName: hello-00002
  percent: 50
Test Traffic Split
for i in {1..10}; do
  curl -s http://hello.default.<EXTERNAL-IP>.nip.io
  echo
done

✔ Output:

Mixed responses:
Hello Knative!
Hello Knative v2!
1️⃣2️⃣ Observe Pods
kubectl get pods -o wide

✔ Both revisions running:

hello-00001
hello-00002
